{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`run_http_with_grace` must not couple uvicorn's `timeout_graceful_shutdown` to the certified-op drain grace. The certified-op drain remains bounded by `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200` and is enforced by `drain_then_exit` over `InFlightGauge`. uvicorn's graceful-shutdown timeout is only a short transport backstop for idle long-lived Streamable-HTTP connections after the gauge is idle.\n\nLatest approved spec is the 2026-09-01 \"DECISION NEEDED\" comment: decouple the two timers, stop new intake on SIGTERM, proactively retire idle streams through a short uvicorn backstop, and preserve the full certified-op grace for in-flight work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `run_http_with_grace` passes uvicorn a short named backstop timeout (not 1200s) that is independent of `grace_seconds`.\n2. `drain_then_exit` continues to use the certified-op grace as the primary bound: idle gauges exit immediately/quickly; busy gauges are allowed to wait until either the gauge drains or the certified-op deadline elapses.\n3. The SIGTERM handler stops new certified-tool intake immediately and only sets `server.should_exit` after the gauge is idle or the certified-op drain deadline expires, so uvicorn's short backstop cannot cut short an in-flight certified op.\n4. Tests prove both directions: an idle-gauge retirement exits well under the 1200s grace, and a busy retirement is not cut short by the short uvicorn backstop and still honors the certified-op drain deadline.\n5. The fix is self-contained in in-process MCP shutdown logic and does not depend on any CI provider or deployment-specific external service.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun focused MCP drain tests plus `make lint` and `make typecheck` before Gerrit push; land only after Gerrit `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788287459520767669,"uuid":"8c2cbb6b-8478-4420-8b64-289afcc9f493"}